            <ArticleTitle>[Pathogenetic aspects of bronchial asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>46-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This review represents contemporary knowledge about pathogenetic aspects of evolvement and progress of human bronchial asthma. Main attention is given to cells and mediators of allergic inflammation, Th1/Th2-bias, remodeling of respiratory tract, genetic and exogenous risk markers. Moreover, opportunities and prospects for the use of laboratory animals in modeling bronchial asthma are assessed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
